 <sect1 id="view-pg-aios">
  <title><structname>pg_aios</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-aios">
   <primary>pg_aios</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_aios</structname> 视图列出当前正在使用的所有 <xref
   linkend="glossary-aio"/> 句柄。I/O 句柄用于引用正在准备、执行或正在完成过程中的 I/O 操作。<structname>pg_aios</structname> 为每个 I/O 句柄包含一行。
  </para>

  <para>
   此视图主要对 <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> 的开发者有用，但在调优
   <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> 时也可能有用。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_aios</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>pid</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       发出此 I/O 的服务器进程的进程 ID。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>io_id</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       I/O 句柄的标识符。一旦 I/O 完成（或者如果在 I/O 开始之前句柄被释放），句柄就会被重用。重用时，
       <link linkend="view-pg-aios-io-generation">
        <structname>pg_aios</structname>.<structfield>io_generation</structfield>
       </link>
       会递增。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry" id="view-pg-aios-io-generation"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>io_generation</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       I/O 句柄的代次。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>state</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       I/O 句柄的状态：
       <itemizedlist>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>HANDED_OUT</literal>，被代码引用但尚未使用
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>DEFINED</literal>，执行所需的信息已知
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>STAGED</literal>，已准备好执行
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>SUBMITTED</literal>，已提交执行
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>COMPLETED_IO</literal>，已完成，但结果尚未处理
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>COMPLETED_SHARED</literal>，共享完成处理已完成
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>COMPLETED_LOCAL</literal>，后端本地完成处理已完成
         </para>
        </listitem>
       </itemizedlist>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>operation</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       使用 I/O 句柄执行的操作：
       <itemizedlist>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>invalid</literal>，尚不清楚
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>readv</literal>，向量化读
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>writev</literal>，向量化写
         </para>
        </listitem>
       </itemizedlist>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>off</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       I/O 操作的偏移量。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>length</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       I/O 操作的长度。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>target</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       I/O 所针对的对象类型：
       <itemizedlist spacing="compact">
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>smgr</literal>，对关系的 I/O
         </para>
        </listitem>
       </itemizedlist>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>handle_data_len</structfield> <type>int2</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       与 I/O 操作相关联的数据长度。对于发往 <xref linkend="guc-shared-buffers"/> 和 <xref
       linkend="guc-temp-buffers"/> 或从它们发出的 I/O，这表示该 I/O 所操作的缓冲区数量。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>raw_result</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       I/O 操作的底层结果，如果操作尚未完成则为 NULL。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>result</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       I/O 操作的高层结果：
       <itemizedlist>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>UNKNOWN</literal> 表示操作结果尚不可知。
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>OK</literal> 表示 I/O 已成功完成。
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>PARTIAL</literal> 表示 I/O 已完成且未出错，但并未处理所有数据。通常调用方需要重试，并在另一次 I/O 中完成剩余的工作。
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>WARNING</literal> 表示 I/O 已完成且没有错误，但执行该 IO 触发了警告。例如，在启用 <xref
          linkend="guc-zero-damaged-pages"/> 时遇到损坏的缓冲区。
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>ERROR</literal> 表示 I/O 因错误而失败。
         </para>
        </listitem>
       </itemizedlist>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>target_desc</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       描述 I/O 操作所针对的目标。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>f_sync</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       指示 I/O 是否同步执行的标志。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>f_localmem</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       指示 I/O 是否引用进程本地内存的标志。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>f_buffered</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       指示 I/O 是否为缓冲 I/O 的标志。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_aios</structname> 视图是只读的。
  </para>

  <para>
   默认情况下，只有超级用户或具有 <literal>pg_read_all_stats</literal> 角色权限的角色才能读取 <structname>pg_aios</structname> 视图。
  </para>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-available-extensions">
  <title><structname>pg_available_extensions</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-available-extensions">
   <primary>pg_available_extensions</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_available_extensions</structname> 视图列出了可供安装的扩展。
   另请参阅
   <link linkend="catalog-pg-extension"><structname>pg_extension</structname></link>
   系统目录，它显示了当前已安装的扩展。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_available_extensions</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>name</structfield> <type>name</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       扩展名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>default_version</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       默认版本的名称，如果未指定则为 <literal>NULL</literal>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>installed_version</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       当前已安装的扩展版本，如果未安装则为 <literal>NULL</literal>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>comment</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       来自扩展控制文件的注释字符串
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_available_extensions</structname> 视图是只读的。
  </para>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-available-extension-versions">
  <title><structname>pg_available_extension_versions</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-available-extension-versions">
   <primary>pg_available_extension_versions</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_available_extension_versions</structname> 视图列出了可供安装的特定扩展版本。
   另请参见 <link
   linkend="catalog-pg-extension"><structname>pg_extension</structname></link>
   系统目录，其中显示了当前已安装的扩展。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_available_extension_versions</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>name</structfield> <type>name</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       扩展名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>version</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       版本名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>installed</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果该扩展的这个版本当前已安装，则为真
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>superuser</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果只允许超级用户安装该扩展，则为真（但参见 <structfield>trusted</structfield>）
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>trusted</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果具有适当权限的非超级用户可以安装该扩展，则为真
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>relocatable</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果扩展可以迁移到另一个模式，则为真
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>schema</structfield> <type>name</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       扩展必须安装到的模式名称；如果可部分或完全迁移，则为 <literal>NULL</literal>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>requires</structfield> <type>name[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       前置扩展的名称；如果没有，则为 <literal>NULL</literal>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>comment</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       来自扩展控制文件的注释字符串
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_available_extension_versions</structname> 视图是只读的。
  </para>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-backend-memory-contexts">
  <title><structname>pg_backend_memory_contexts</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-backend-memory-contexts">
   <primary>pg_backend_memory_contexts</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_backend_memory_contexts</structname> 显示附加到当前会话的服务器进程的所有内存上下文。
  </para>
  <para>
   <structname>pg_backend_memory_contexts</structname> 为每个内存上下文包含一行。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_backend_memory_contexts</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>name</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       内存上下文的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>ident</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       内存上下文的标识信息。此字段截断至 1024 字节
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>type</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       内存上下文的类型
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>level</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       该上下文在内存上下文层次结构中的层级（从 1 开始）。上下文的层级还显示了该上下文在 <structfield>path</structfield> 列中的位置。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>path</structfield> <type>int4[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       用于描述内存上下文层次结构的临时数字标识符数组。第一个元素对应 <literal>TopMemoryContext</literal>，后续元素包含中间父级，最后一个元素包含当前上下文的标识符。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>total_bytes</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       为此内存上下文分配的总字节数
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>total_nblocks</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       为此内存上下文分配的总块数
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>free_bytes</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       空闲空间（字节）
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>free_chunks</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       空闲块总数
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>used_bytes</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       已用空间（字节）
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   默认情况下，只有超级用户或具有 <literal>pg_read_all_stats</literal> 角色权限的角色才能读取 <structname>pg_backend_memory_contexts</structname> 视图。
  </para>

  <para>
   由于内存上下文是在查询运行期间创建和销毁的，因此 <structfield>path</structfield> 列中存储的标识符在同一查询中多次调用该视图之间可能不稳定。下面的示例演示了该列的有效用法，并计算 <literal>CacheMemoryContext</literal> 及其所有子上下文所使用的总字节数：

<programlisting>
WITH memory_contexts AS (
    SELECT * FROM pg_backend_memory_contexts
)
SELECT sum(c1.total_bytes)
FROM memory_contexts c1, memory_contexts c2
WHERE c2.name = 'CacheMemoryContext'
AND c1.path[c2.level] = c2.path[c2.level];
</programlisting>

   这里使用<link linkend="queries-with">公共表表达式</link>来确保 <structfield>path</structfield> 列中的上下文 ID 在该视图的两次求值之间保持一致。
  </para>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-config">
  <title><structname>pg_config</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-config">
   <primary>pg_config</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_config</structname> 描述了
   当前安装的 <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> 版本的
   编译时配置参数。例如，它旨在
   供希望与 <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> 对接的软件包使用，
   以便于查找所需的头
   文件和库。它提供的基本信息与
   <xref linkend="app-pgconfig"/> <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> 客户端
   应用相同。
  </para>

  <para>
   默认情况下，只有超级用户才能读取
   视图 <structname>pg_config</structname>。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_config</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>name</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       参数名
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>setting</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       参数值
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-cursors">
  <title><structname>pg_cursors</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-cursors">
   <primary>pg_cursors</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_cursors</structname> 视图列出当前可用的游标。游标可以通过几种方式定义：
   <itemizedlist>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      通过 SQL 中的 <link linkend="sql-declare"><command>DECLARE</command></link> 语句
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
     <para>
      通过前端/后端协议中的 Bind 消息，如 <xref linkend="protocol-flow-ext-query"/> 所述
     </para>
    </listitem>

    <listitem>
     <para>
      通过服务器编程接口（SPI），如 <xref linkend="spi-interface"/> 所述
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </itemizedlist>

   <structname>pg_cursors</structname> 视图显示通过上述任一方式创建的游标。游标仅在定义它们的事务持续期间存在，除非它们已被声明为 <literal>WITH HOLD</literal>。因此，非保持型游标只在其创建事务结束之前出现在该视图中。

   <note>
    <para>
     游标在内部被用于实现 <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> 的某些组件，例如过程语言。因此，<structname>pg_cursors</structname> 视图可能包含并非由用户显式创建的游标。
    </para>
   </note>
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_cursors</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>name</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       游标的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>statement</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       提交用于声明该游标的原始查询字符串
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>is_holdable</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果游标可保持（即，在声明该游标的事务提交之后仍可访问），则为 <literal>true</literal>；否则为 <literal>false</literal>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>is_binary</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       <literal>true</literal>，如果游标被声明为
       <literal>BINARY</literal>；否则为 <literal>false</literal>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>is_scrollable</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       <literal>true</literal>，如果游标是可滚动的（即
       允许以非顺序方式检索行）；
       否则为 <literal>false</literal>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>creation_time</structfield> <type>timestamptz</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       游标被声明的时间
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_cursors</structname> 视图是只读的。
  </para>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-file-settings">
  <title><structname>pg_file_settings</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-file-settings">
   <primary>pg_file_settings</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_file_settings</structname> 提供服务器配置文件内容的摘要。文件中每个 <quote>name = value</quote> 条目都会在此视图中对应一行，并带有注释说明该值是否能够成功应用。对于与 <quote>name = value</quote> 条目无关的问题（例如文件中的语法错误），可能会出现额外的行。
  </para>

  <para>
   此视图有助于检查配置文件中的计划变更是否会生效，或用于诊断先前的失败。请注意，此视图报告的是文件的<emphasis>当前</emphasis>内容，而不是服务器上次应用的内容。（<link linkend="view-pg-settings"><structname>pg_settings</structname></link> 视图通常足以确定这一点。）
  </para>

  <para>
   默认情况下，只有超级用户才能读取 <structname>pg_file_settings</structname> 视图。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_file_settings</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>sourcefile</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       配置文件的完整路径名
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>sourceline</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       该条目在配置文件中出现的行号
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>seqno</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       条目的处理顺序（1..<replaceable>n</replaceable>）
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>name</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       配置参数名
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>setting</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       要赋给参数的值
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>applied</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果该值可以成功应用则为真
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>error</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果不为空，则表示一条错误消息，说明此条目为何无法被应用
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   如果配置文件包含语法错误或无效的参数名，服务器将不会尝试应用其中的任何设置，因此所有 <structfield>applied</structfield> 字段都会读为 false。
   在这种情况下，会有一行或多行具有非空的 <structfield>error</structfield> 字段，指出问题所在。否则，将尽可能应用各个设置。
   如果某个单独设置无法应用（例如值无效，或该设置在服务器启动后无法更改），它将在 <structfield>error</structfield> 字段中给出相应的消息。
   条目出现 <structfield>applied</structfield> = false 的另一种可能是，它被同一参数名的后续条目覆盖；这种情况不被视为错误，因此 <structfield>error</structfield> 字段中不会显示任何内容。
  </para>

  <para>
   有关更改运行时参数的各种方式的更多信息，请参见 <xref linkend="config-setting"/>。
  </para>

</sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-group">
  <title><structname>pg_group</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-group">
   <primary>pg_group</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <!-- Unlike information_schema.applicable_roles, this shows no members for
       pg_database_owner.  The v8.1 catalog would have shown no members if
       that role had existed at the time. -->
  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_group</structname> 是为了向后兼容而存在的：它模拟了 8.1 版本之前 <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> 中存在的一个系统目录。
   它显示了所有被标记为不是 <structfield>rolcanlogin</structfield> 的角色的名称和成员，
   这是对正在被用作组的角色集合的一种近似。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_group</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>groname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>.<structfield>rolname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       组的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>grosysid</structfield> <type>oid</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>.<structfield>oid</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       此组的 ID
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>grolist</structfield> <type>oid[]</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>.<structfield>oid</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       一个数组，包含此组中角色的 ID
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-hba-file-rules">
  <title><structname>pg_hba_file_rules</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-hba-file-rules">
   <primary>pg_hba_file_rules</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_hba_file_rules</structname> 提供了客户端认证配置文件 <link linkend="auth-pg-hba-conf"><filename>pg_hba.conf</filename></link> 的内容摘要。
   该文件中的每个非空、非注释行都会在此视图中对应一行，
   并附带标注说明该规则是否能够成功应用。
  </para>

  <para>
   此视图有助于检查认证配置文件中计划的更改是否可行，或用于诊断之前的失败。
   请注意，此视图报告的是文件的<emphasis>当前</emphasis>内容，而不是服务器最后加载的内容。
  </para>

  <para>
   默认情况下，只有超级用户可以读取 <structname>pg_hba_file_rules</structname> 视图。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_hba_file_rules</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rule_number</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此规则的编号（如果有效），否则为 <literal>NULL</literal>。
       这表示在认证过程中，在找到匹配项之前，考虑每条规则的顺序。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>file_name</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       包含此规则的文件名
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>line_number</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此规则在 <literal>file_name</literal> 中的行号
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>type</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       连接类型
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>database</structfield> <type>text[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此规则适用的数据库名称列表
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>user_name</structfield> <type>text[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此规则适用的用户和组名称列表
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>address</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       主机名或 IP 地址，或者 <literal>all</literal>、<literal>samehost</literal> 或 <literal>samenet</literal> 之一，对于本地连接则为 null
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>netmask</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       IP 地址掩码，如果不适用则为 null
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>auth_method</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       认证方法
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>options</structfield> <type>text[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       为认证方法指定的选项（如果有）
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>error</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果不为 null，则是一条错误消息，说明为什么无法处理此行
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   通常，反映错误条目的行将只包含 <structfield>line_number</structfield> 和 <structfield>error</structfield> 字段的值。
  </para>

  <para>
   有关客户端认证配置的更多信息，请参见 <xref linkend="client-authentication"/>。
  </para>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-ident-file-mappings">
  <title><structname>pg_ident_file_mappings</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-ident-file-mappings">
   <primary>pg_ident_file_mappings</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_ident_file_mappings</structname> 提供了客户端用户名映射配置文件 <link linkend="auth-username-maps"><filename>pg_ident.conf</filename></link> 内容的摘要。该文件中的每个非空、非注释行都会在此视图中显示为一行，并附带标注说明该映射是否能够成功应用。
  </para>

  <para>
   此视图有助于检查认证配置文件中的计划变更是否会生效，或用于诊断之前的失败。请注意，此视图报告的是文件的<emphasis>当前</emphasis>内容，而不是服务器上次加载的内容。
  </para>

  <para>
   默认情况下，只有超级用户可以读取 <structname>pg_ident_file_mappings</structname> 视图。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_ident_file_mappings</structname> 列</title> <tgroup
   cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>map_number</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此映射的编号，按优先级顺序排列（如果有效），否则为
       <literal>NULL</literal>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>file_name</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       包含此映射的文件名
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>line_number</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此映射在 <literal>file_name</literal> 中的行号
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>map_name</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       映射的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>sys_name</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       检测到的客户端用户名
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>pg_username</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       请求的 PostgreSQL 用户名
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>error</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果未设置 <literal>NULL</literal>，则显示一条错误消息，说明为什么这一行无法被处理
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   通常，反映错误条目的一行只会包含 <structfield>line_number</structfield> 和 <structfield>error</structfield> 字段的值。
  </para>

  <para>
   有关客户端认证配置的更多信息，请参见 <xref linkend="client-authentication"/>。
  </para>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-indexes">
  <title><structname>pg_indexes</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-indexes">
   <primary>pg_indexes</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_indexes</structname> 提供了对数据库中每个索引的有用信息的访问。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_indexes</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>schemaname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>nspname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       包含表和索引的模式名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>tablename</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>relname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       该索引所属的表的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>indexname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>relname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       索引的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>tablespace</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-tablespace"><structname>pg_tablespace</structname></link>.<structfield>spcname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       包含该索引的表空间的名称（如果使用数据库的默认表空间则为空）
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>indexdef</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       索引定义（重建的 <xref linkend="sql-createindex"/> 命令）
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-locks">
  <title><structname>pg_locks</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-locks">
   <primary>pg_locks</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_locks</structname> 提供对数据库服务器中活动进程所持有的锁的相关信息的访问。关于锁定的更多讨论，请参见 <xref linkend="mvcc"/>。
  </para>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_locks</structname> 为每个活动的可锁定对象、请求的锁模式以及相关进程各包含一行。因此，如果多个进程持有或等待某个可锁定对象上的锁，那么同一个可锁定对象可能会出现多次。不过，当前没有任何锁的对象根本不会出现。
  </para>

  <para>
   可锁定对象有几种不同的类型：整个关系（例如表）、关系的各个页面、关系的各个元组、事务 ID（包括虚拟 ID 和永久 ID），以及通用数据库对象（通过类 OID 和对象 OID 来标识，方式与 <link linkend="catalog-pg-description"><structname>pg_description</structname></link> 或 <link linkend="catalog-pg-depend"><structname>pg_depend</structname></link> 中相同）。此外，扩展关系的权利被表示为一个单独的可锁定对象，更新 <structname>pg_database</structname>.<structfield>datfrozenxid</structfield> 的权利也是如此。另外，还可以对具有用户自定义含义的数字获取<quote>咨询</quote>锁。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_locks</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>locktype</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       可锁定对象的类型：
       <literal>relation</literal>、
       <literal>extend</literal>、
       <literal>frozenid</literal>、
       <literal>page</literal>、
       <literal>tuple</literal>、
       <literal>transactionid</literal>、
       <literal>virtualxid</literal>、
       <literal>spectoken</literal>、
       <literal>object</literal>、
       <literal>userlock</literal>、
       <literal>advisory</literal> 或
       <literal>applytransaction</literal>。
       （另请参见 <xref linkend="wait-event-lock-table"/>。）
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>database</structfield> <type>oid</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-database"><structname>pg_database</structname></link>.<structfield>oid</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       锁目标所在数据库的 OID；如果目标是共享对象，则为零；
       如果目标是事务 ID，则为空
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>relation</structfield> <type>oid</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>oid</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       锁所针对的关系的 OID；如果目标不是关系或关系的一部分，则为空
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>page</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       锁在关系内所针对的页号；
       如果目标不是关系页或元组，则为空
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>tuple</structfield> <type>int2</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       锁在页内所针对的元组号，如果目标不是元组则为 null
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>virtualxid</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       锁所针对的事务的虚拟 ID，如果目标不是虚拟事务 ID 则为 null；参见
<xref linkend="transactions"/>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>transactionid</structfield> <type>xid</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       锁所针对的事务的 ID，如果目标不是事务 ID 则为 null；<xref linkend="transactions"/>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>classid</structfield> <type>oid</type>
（引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>oid</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       包含锁目标的系统目录的 OID，如果目标不是普通数据库对象则为 null
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>objid</structfield> <type>oid</type>
（引用任意 OID 列）
      </para>
      <para>
       锁目标在其系统目录中的 OID，如果目标不是普通数据库对象则为 null
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>objsubid</structfield> <type>int2</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       锁所针对的列号（<structfield>classid</structfield> 和 <structfield>objid</structfield> 指表本身），如果目标是其他某种普通数据库对象则为零，如果目标不是普通数据库对象则为 null
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>virtualtransaction</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       持有或等待此锁的事务的虚拟 ID
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>pid</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       持有或等待此锁的服务器进程的进程 ID，如果该锁由预备事务持有则为 null
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>mode</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此进程持有或期望的锁模式的名称（参见 <xref linkend="locking-tables"/> 和 <xref linkend="xact-serializable"/>）
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>granted</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果锁已被持有则为 true，如果正在等待锁则为 false
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>fastpath</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果锁是通过快速路径获得的则为真，如果通过主锁表获得的则为假
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>waitstart</structfield> <type>timestamptz</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       服务器进程开始等待此锁的时间，
       如果该锁已被持有则为 null。
       注意，在等待开始后的极短时间内，即使 <structfield>granted</structfield>
       为 <literal>false</literal>，该值也可能为 null。
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   在表示由所指示进程持有的锁的行中，<structfield>granted</structfield> 为真。
   假表示该进程当前正在等待获取此锁，这意味着至少有一个
   其他进程在同一可锁定对象上持有或等待冲突的锁模式。等待的进程
   将休眠，直到其他锁被释放（或检测到死锁情况）。单个进程
   一次最多只能等待获取一个锁。
  </para>

  <para>
   在事务运行的整个过程中，服务器进程持有该事务的虚拟事务 ID 上的排他锁。
   如果为该事务分配了永久 ID（通常仅在事务改变数据库状态时才会发生），
   它还会持有该事务的永久事务 ID 上的排他锁，直到事务结束。当进程发现
   有必要专门等待另一个事务结束时，它会尝试获取另一个事务 ID
   （根据情况是虚拟 ID 还是永久 ID）上的共享锁来实现等待。只有当另一个
   事务终止并释放其锁时，该尝试才会成功。
  </para>

  <para>
   尽管元组是一种可锁定的对象类型，
   但行级锁的信息存储在磁盘上而非内存中，
   因此行级锁通常不会出现在此视图中。
   如果某个进程正在等待
   行级锁，它通常会在此视图中显示为等待该行锁当前持有者的
   永久事务 ID。
  </para>

  <para>
   推测性插入锁由一个事务 ID 和一个推测性插入令牌组成。推测性插入令牌
   显示在 <structfield>objid</structfield> 列中。
  </para>

  <para>
   咨询锁可以基于由单个 <type>bigint</type> 值或两个整数值构成的键来获取。
   一个 <type>bigint</type> 键的显示方式是：其高位部分位于 <structfield>classid</structfield> 列，低位部分
   位于 <structfield>objid</structfield> 列，而 <structfield>objsubid</structfield> 等于 1。原始的 <type>bigint</type> 值可以用
   表达式 <literal>(classid::bigint &lt;&lt; 32) |
   objid::bigint</literal> 重新组合出来。整数键的显示方式是：第一个键位于
   <structfield>classid</structfield> 列，第二个键位于 <structfield>objid</structfield> 列，而 <structfield>objsubid</structfield> 等于 2。这些键的
   实际含义由用户自行决定。咨询锁是各数据库本地的，
   因此 <structfield>database</structfield> 列对咨询锁是有意义的。
  </para>

  <para>
   应用事务锁在并行模式下用于在逻辑复制中应用事务。远程事务 ID 显示在
   <structfield>transactionid</structfield> 列中。<structfield>objsubid</structfield>
   显示锁的子类型：0 表示用于同步变更集的锁，1 表示用于等待事务
   完成以确保提交顺序的锁。
  </para>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_locks</structname> 提供数据库集簇中所有锁的全局视图，而不仅仅是与当前数据库
   相关的那些锁。尽管它的 <structfield>relation</structfield> 列可以与
   <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>oid</structfield> 连接以标识被锁定的
   关系，但这仅对当前数据库中的关系（即 <structfield>database</structfield> 列为当前数据库的 OID
   或零的那些关系）才能正确工作。
  </para>

  <para>
   <structfield>pid</structfield> 列可以与
   <link linkend="monitoring-pg-stat-activity-view">
   <structname>pg_stat_activity</structname></link>
   视图的 <structfield>pid</structfield> 列连接，以获取有关持有或等待每个锁的会话的更多
   信息，例如
<programlisting>
SELECT * FROM pg_locks pl LEFT JOIN pg_stat_activity psa
    ON pl.pid = psa.pid;
</programlisting>
   另外，如果您使用了预备事务，则 <structfield>virtualtransaction</structfield> 列可以与
   <link
   linkend="view-pg-prepared-xacts"><structname>pg_prepared_xacts</structname></link>
   视图的 <structfield>transaction</structfield> 列连接，以获取有关持有锁的预备事务的更多信息。
   （预备事务永远不会在等待锁，但它会继续持有其在运行期间获取的锁。）
   例如：
<programlisting>
SELECT * FROM pg_locks pl LEFT JOIN pg_prepared_xacts ppx
    ON pl.virtualtransaction = '-1/' || ppx.transaction;
</programlisting>
  </para>

  <para>
   虽然通过将 <structname>pg_locks</structname> 与自身连接可以获得关于哪些进程阻塞了哪些其他进程的信息，但要在细节上做到正确是非常困难的。这样的查询必须编码关于哪些锁模式与哪些锁模式冲突的知识。更糟的是，<structname>pg_locks</structname> 视图并不暴露哪些进程在锁等待队列中排在哪些进程之前的信息，也不暴露哪些进程是代表哪些其他客户端会话运行的并行工作进程的信息。最好使用 <function>pg_blocking_pids()</function> 函数（参见 <xref linkend="functions-info-session-table"/>）来确定某个正在等待的进程被哪些进程阻塞。
  </para>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_locks</structname> 视图显示来自常规锁管理器和谓词锁管理器的数据，这两个是彼此独立的系统；此外，常规锁管理器还将其锁细分为常规锁和<firstterm>快速路径</firstterm>锁。不保证这些数据完全一致。查询该视图时，关于快速路径锁（<structfield>fastpath</structfield> = <literal>true</literal>）的数据是逐个从每个后端收集的，期间不会冻结整个锁管理器的状态，因此在收集信息的过程中锁可能被获取或释放。但请注意，已知这些锁不会与当前持有的任何其他锁冲突。在向所有后端查询完快速路径锁之后，常规锁管理器的其余部分会作为一个整体被锁定，并以原子操作的方式收集所有剩余锁的一致快照。解除对常规锁管理器的锁定后，谓词锁管理器同样被锁定，并以原子操作的方式收集所有谓词锁。因此，除快速路径锁之外，每个锁管理器都会提供一组一致的结果，但由于我们并不同时锁定两个锁管理器，在我们查询常规锁管理器之后、查询谓词锁管理器之前，锁仍可能被获取或释放。
  </para>

  <para>
   如果非常频繁地访问该视图，锁定常规锁管理器和/或谓词锁管理器可能会对数据库性能产生一些影响。锁只会在从锁管理器获取数据所需的最短时间内持有，但这并不能完全消除性能受到影响的可能性。
  </para>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-matviews">
  <title><structname>pg_matviews</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-matviews">
   <primary>pg_matviews</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-matviews">
   <primary>materialized views</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_matviews</structname> 提供了对数据库中每个物化视图的有用信息的访问。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_matviews</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>schemaname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>nspname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       包含该物化视图的模式名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>matviewname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>relname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       物化视图的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>matviewowner</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>.<structfield>rolname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       物化视图拥有者的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>tablespace</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-tablespace"><structname>pg_tablespace</structname></link>.<structfield>spcname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       包含该物化视图的表空间的名称（如果为数据库的默认表空间则为 null）
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>hasindexes</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果物化视图有（或最近有过）任何索引，则为真
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>ispopulated</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果物化视图当前已填充，则为真
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>definition</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       物化视图定义（重建的 <xref linkend="sql-select"/> 查询）
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-policies">
  <title><structname>pg_policies</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-policies">
   <primary>pg_policies</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_policies</structname> 提供对数据库中每个行级安全策略的有用信息的访问。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_policies</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>schemaname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>nspname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       策略所在表所属模式的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>tablename</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>relname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       策略所在的表名
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>policyname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-policy"><structname>pg_policy</structname></link>.<structfield>polname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       策略的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>permissive</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       该策略是宽容型还是限制型？
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>roles</structfield> <type>name[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       该策略适用的角色
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>cmd</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       该策略所应用到的命令类型
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>qual</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       为应用此策略的查询添加到安全屏障限定条件中的表达式
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>with_check</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       为尝试向此表添加行的查询添加到 WITH CHECK 限定条件中的表达式
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-prepared-statements">
  <title><structname>pg_prepared_statements</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-prepared-statements">
   <primary>pg_prepared_statements</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_prepared_statements</structname> 视图显示当前会话中所有可用的预备语句。有关预备语句的更多信息，请参见 <xref linkend="sql-prepare"/>。
  </para>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_prepared_statements</structname> 为每个预备语句包含一行。当创建新的预备语句时，行会被添加到该视图中；当释放预备语句时（例如通过 <link linkend="sql-deallocate"><command>DEALLOCATE</command></link> 命令），行会被移除。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_prepared_statements</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>name</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       预备语句的标识符
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>statement</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       客户端为创建这个预备语句而提交的查询字符串。对于通过 SQL 创建的预备语句，这是客户端提交的 <command>PREPARE</command> 语句。对于通过前端/后端协议创建的预备语句，这是预备语句本身的文本。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>prepare_time</structfield> <type>timestamptz</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       预备语句创建的时间
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>parameter_types</structfield> <type>regtype[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       预备语句的预期参数类型，以 <type>regtype</type> 数组的形式表示。该数组中某个元素对应的 OID 可以通过将 <type>regtype</type> 值转换为 <type>oid</type> 来获得。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>result_types</structfield> <type>regtype[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       预备语句返回的列类型，以 <type>regtype</type> 数组的形式表示。该数组中某个元素对应的 OID 可以通过将 <type>regtype</type> 值转换为 <type>oid</type> 来获得。如果预备语句不提供结果（例如 DML 语句），则该字段为 null。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>from_sql</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果预备语句是通过 <command>PREPARE</command> SQL 命令创建的，则为 <literal>true</literal>；如果该语句是通过前端/后端协议预备的，则为 <literal>false</literal>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>generic_plans</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       选择通用计划的次数
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>custom_plans</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       自定义计划被选择的次数
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_prepared_statements</structname> 视图是只读的。
  </para>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-prepared-xacts">
  <title><structname>pg_prepared_xacts</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-prepared-xacts">
   <primary>pg_prepared_xacts</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_prepared_xacts</structname> 显示当前为两阶段提交而预备的事务的信息（详见 <xref linkend="sql-prepare-transaction"/>）。
  </para>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_prepared_xacts</structname> 中每个预备事务占一行。当事务被提交或回滚时，相应的条目会被移除。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_prepared_xacts</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>transaction</structfield> <type>xid</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       预备事务的数字事务标识符
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>gid</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       分配给该事务的全局事务标识符
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>prepared</structfield> <type>timestamptz</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       该事务准备提交的时间
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>owner</structfield> <type>name</type>
（引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>.<structfield>rolname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       执行该事务的用户的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>database</structfield> <type>name</type>
（引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-database"><structname>pg_database</structname></link>.<structfield>datname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       执行该事务所在的数据库的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   访问 <structname>pg_prepared_xacts</structname> 视图时，内部事务管理器数据结构会被短暂锁定，并复制一份供视图显示。这确保视图产生一致的结果集，同时不会不必要地长时间阻塞正常操作。尽管如此，如果频繁访问此视图，可能会对数据库性能产生一定影响。
  </para>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-publication-tables">
  <title><structname>pg_publication_tables</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-publication-tables">
   <primary>pg_publication_tables</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_publication_tables</structname> 提供关于发布与它们所包含的表的信息之间的映射的信息。与底层的系统目录
   <link linkend="catalog-pg-publication-rel"><structname>pg_publication_rel</structname></link> 不同，
   此视图会展开定义为
   <link linkend="sql-createpublication-params-for-all-tables"><literal>FOR ALL TABLES</literal></link>
   和 <link linkend="sql-createpublication-params-for-tables-in-schema"><literal>FOR TABLES IN SCHEMA</literal></link>
   的发布，因此对于此类发布，每个符合条件的表都会有一行。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_publication_tables</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>pubname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-publication"><structname>pg_publication</structname></link>.<structfield>pubname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       发布的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>schemaname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>nspname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       包含该表的模式的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>tablename</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>relname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       表的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>attnames</structfield> <type>name[]</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-attribute"><structname>pg_attribute</structname></link>.<structfield>attname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       包含在发布中的表列的名称。当用户没有为该表指定列列表时，这里包含该表的所有列。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rowfilter</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       表的发布限定条件的表达式
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>
 </sect1>

  <sect1 id="view-pg-replication-origin-status">
  <title><structname>pg_replication_origin_status</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-replication-origin-status">
   <primary>pg_replication_origin_status</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_replication_origin_status</structname> 视图包含有关某个源的回放进度信息。有关复制源的更多信息，请参见 <xref linkend="replication-origins"/>。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_replication_origin_status</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>local_id</structfield> <type>oid</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-replication-origin"><structname>pg_replication_origin</structname></link>.<structfield>roident</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       内部节点标识符
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>external_id</structfield> <type>text</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-replication-origin"><structname>pg_replication_origin</structname></link>.<structfield>roname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       外部节点标识符
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>remote_lsn</structfield> <type>pg_lsn</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       源节点的 LSN，数据已复制到该位置。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>local_lsn</structfield> <type>pg_lsn</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       本节点的 LSN，<literal>remote_lsn</literal> 已复制到该位置。在使用异步提交时，用于在将数据持久化到磁盘之前刷写提交记录。
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-replication-slots">
  <title><structname>pg_replication_slots</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-replication-slots">
   <primary>pg_replication_slots</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_replication_slots</structname> 视图列出了数据库集簇中当前存在的所有复制槽及其当前状态。
  </para>

  <para>
   关于复制槽的更多信息，请参见 <xref linkend="streaming-replication-slots"/> 和 <xref linkend="logicaldecoding"/>。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_replication_slots</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>slot_name</structfield> <type>name</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       复制槽在集簇范围内唯一的标识符
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>plugin</structfield> <type>name</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       该逻辑槽所使用的、包含输出插件的共享对象的基本名称；对于物理槽则为 null。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>slot_type</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       槽类型：<literal>physical</literal> 或 <literal>logical</literal>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>datoid</structfield> <type>oid</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-database"><structname>pg_database</structname></link>.<structfield>oid</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       该槽所关联的数据库的 OID，或 null。只有逻辑槽才有关联的数据库。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>database</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-database"><structname>pg_database</structname></link>.<structfield>datname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       该槽所关联的数据库的名称，或 null。只有逻辑槽才有关联的数据库。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>temporary</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果这是一个临时复制槽，则为真。临时槽不会保存到磁盘，并且在出错或会话结束时会被自动删除。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>active</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果此槽当前正在被流式传输，则为真
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>active_pid</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       为该槽流式传输数据的会话的进程 ID。如果不活动，则为 <literal>NULL</literal>。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>xmin</structfield> <type>xid</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此槽需要数据库保留的最旧事务。<literal>VACUUM</literal> 无法移除被任何更晚的事务删除的元组。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>catalog_xmin</structfield> <type>xid</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此槽需要数据库保留的影响系统目录的最旧事务。<literal>VACUUM</literal> 无法移除被任何更晚的事务删除的目录元组。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>restart_lsn</structfield> <type>pg_lsn</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此槽的消费者仍可能需要的最旧 WAL 的地址（<literal>LSN</literal>），因此在检查点期间不会被自动移除，除非该 LSN 落后当前 LSN 超过 <xref linkend="guc-max-slot-wal-keep-size"/>。如果此槽的 <literal>LSN</literal> 从未被保留，则为 <literal>NULL</literal>。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>confirmed_flush_lsn</structfield> <type>pg_lsn</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       逻辑槽的消费者已确认接收到数据的地址（<literal>LSN</literal>）。与此 <literal>LSN</literal> 之前提交的事务相对应的数据不再可用。对于物理槽为 <literal>NULL</literal>。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>wal_status</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此槽所声称的 WAL 文件的可用性。可能的值为：
       <itemizedlist>
        <listitem>
         <para><literal>reserved</literal> 表示所声称的文件在 <varname>max_wal_size</varname> 之内。</para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para><literal>extended</literal> 表示已超出 <varname>max_wal_size</varname>，但文件仍被保留，或者由复制槽保留，或者由 <varname>wal_keep_size</varname> 保留。
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>unreserved</literal> 表示该槽不再保留所需的 WAL 文件，其中一些文件将在下一次检查点时被移除。这通常发生在 <xref linkend="guc-max-slot-wal-keep-size"/> 被设置为非负值时。此状态可以返回到 <literal>reserved</literal> 或 <literal>extended</literal>。
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>lost</literal> 表示该槽不再可用。
         </para>
        </listitem>
       </itemizedlist>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>safe_wal_size</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       可以写入 WAL 的字节数，使得该槽不会面临进入“lost”状态的危险。对于已丢失的槽，以及当 <varname>max_slot_wal_keep_size</varname> 为 <literal>-1</literal> 时，该值为 NULL。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>two_phase</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果该槽启用了对预备事务的解码，则为 true。对于物理槽始终为 false。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>two_phase_at</structfield> <type>pg_lsn</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       启用预备事务解码的地址（<literal>LSN</literal>）。对于 <structfield>two_phase</structfield> 为 false 的逻辑槽以及物理槽，为 <literal>NULL</literal>。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>inactive_since</structfield> <type>timestamptz</type>
      </para>
      <para>
        该槽变为非活动状态的时间。如果该槽当前正在被流式传输，则为 <literal>NULL</literal>。如果该槽变为无效，此值将永远不会被更新。
        对于正在从主服务器（其 <structfield>synced</structfield> 字段为 <literal>true</literal>）同步的备用槽，<structfield>inactive_since</structfield>
        表示最近一次停止槽同步（参见 <xref
        linkend="logicaldecoding-replication-slots-synchronization"/>）的时间。如果该槽一直处于同步状态，则为 <literal>NULL</literal>。这有助于备用槽跟踪同步被中断的时间。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>conflicting</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果该逻辑槽与恢复发生冲突（因而现在已失效），则为 true。当此列为 true 时，请查看
       <structfield>invalidation_reason</structfield> 列以了解冲突原因。对于物理槽始终为 <literal>NULL</literal>。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>invalidation_reason</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       该槽失效的原因。逻辑槽和物理槽都会设置该值。如果该槽未失效，则为 <literal>NULL</literal>。
       可能的值为：
       <itemizedlist spacing="compact">
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>wal_removed</literal> 表示所需的 WAL 已被移除。
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>rows_removed</literal> 表示所需的行已被移除。该字段仅对逻辑槽设置。
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>wal_level_insufficient</literal> 表示主库没有足以执行逻辑解码的
          <xref linkend="guc-wal-level"/>。该字段仅对逻辑槽设置。
         </para>
        </listitem>
        <listitem>
         <para>
          <literal>idle_timeout</literal> 表示该槽处于非活动状态的时间已超过配置的
          <xref linkend="guc-idle-replication-slot-timeout"/> 时长。
         </para>
        </listitem>
       </itemizedlist>
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>failover</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果这是一个已启用同步到备库的逻辑槽，从而在故障转移后可以从新的主库恢复逻辑复制，则为 true。对于物理槽始终为 false。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>synced</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       如果这是一个从主服务器同步而来的逻辑槽，则为 true。在热备库上，synced 列标记为 true 的槽既不能用于逻辑解码，也不能手动删除。该列的值在主服务器上没有意义；主服务器上该列的值对所有槽默认为 false，但也可能为 true（如果是从被提升的备库遗留的）。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-roles">
  <title><structname>pg_roles</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-roles">
   <primary>pg_roles</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_roles</structname> 提供对数据库角色信息的访问。它实际上就是 <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link> 的一个可公开读取的视图，其中密码字段被清空。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_roles</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rolname</structfield> <type>name</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       角色名
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rolsuper</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       角色具有超级用户权限
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rolinherit</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       角色自动继承其所属角色的权限
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rolcreaterole</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       角色可以创建更多角色
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rolcreatedb</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       角色可以创建数据库
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rolcanlogin</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       角色可以登录。也就是说，此角色可以作为初始会话授权标识符
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rolreplication</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       角色是复制角色。复制角色可以发起复制连接，并创建和删除复制槽。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rolconnlimit</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       对于可以登录的角色，此设置指定该角色可以建立的最大并发连接数。-1 表示不限制。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rolpassword</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       不是密码（始终读作 <literal>********</literal>）
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rolvaliduntil</structfield> <type>timestamptz</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       密码过期时间（仅用于密码认证）；如果没有过期时间则为 null
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rolbypassrls</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       角色绕过所有行级安全策略，更多信息请参见 <xref linkend="ddl-rowsecurity"/>。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rolconfig</structfield> <type>text[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       角色特定的运行时配置变量默认值
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>oid</structfield> <type>oid</type>
（引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>.<structfield>oid</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       角色的 ID
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-rules">
  <title><structname>pg_rules</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-rules">
   <primary>pg_rules</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_rules</structname> 提供了对查询重写规则相关有用信息的访问。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_rules</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>schemaname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>nspname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       包含该表的模式的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>tablename</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>relname</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       该规则所针对的表的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>rulename</structfield> <type>name</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-rewrite"><structname>pg_rewrite</structname></link>.<structfield>rulename</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       规则的名称
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>definition</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       规则定义（重建的创建命令）
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_rules</structname> 视图不包含视图和物化视图的 <literal>ON SELECT</literal> 规则；这些规则可以在
   <link linkend="view-pg-views"><structname>pg_views</structname></link> 和 <link linkend="view-pg-matviews"><structname>pg_matviews</structname></link> 中看到。
  </para>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-seclabels">
  <title><structname>pg_seclabels</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-seclabels">
   <primary>pg_seclabels</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   视图 <structname>pg_seclabels</structname> 提供关于安全标签的信息。它是
   <link linkend="catalog-pg-seclabel"><structname>pg_seclabel</structname></link> 系统目录的一个更易于查询的版本。
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_seclabels</structname> 列</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       列类型
      </para>
      <para>
       描述
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>objoid</structfield> <type>oid</type>
       （引用任意 OID 列）
      </para>
      <para>
       此安全标签所涉及对象的 OID
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>classoid</structfield> <type>oid</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>oid</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       该对象所在的系统目录的 OID
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>objsubid</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       对于表列上的安全标签，这是列号（<structfield>objoid</structfield> 和 <structfield>classoid</structfield> 指的是表本身）。对于所有其他对象类型，此列为零。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>objtype</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此标签所适用的对象类型，以文本形式表示。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>objnamespace</structfield> <type>oid</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>oid</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       此对象所属命名空间的 OID（如果适用）；否则为 NULL。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>objname</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       此标签所适用对象的名称，为文本类型。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>provider</structfield> <type>text</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-seclabel"><structname>pg_seclabel</structname></link>.<structfield>provider</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       与此标签关联的标签提供者。
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>label</structfield> <type>text</type>
       （引用 <link linkend="catalog-pg-seclabel"><structname>pg_seclabel</structname></link>.<structfield>label</structfield>）
      </para>
      <para>
       应用于此对象的安全标签。
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-sequences">
  <title><structname>pg_sequences</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-sequences">
   <primary>pg_sequences</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   The view <structname>pg_sequences</structname> provides access to
   useful information about each sequence in the database.
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_sequences</structname> Columns</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       Column Type
      </para>
      <para>
       Description
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>schemaname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>nspname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of schema containing sequence
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>sequencename</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>relname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of sequence
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>sequenceowner</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>.<structfield>rolname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of sequence's owner
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>data_type</structfield> <type>regtype</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-type"><structname>pg_type</structname></link>.<structfield>oid</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Data type of the sequence
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>start_value</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Start value of the sequence
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>min_value</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Minimum value of the sequence
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>max_value</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Maximum value of the sequence
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>increment_by</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Increment value of the sequence
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>cycle</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Whether the sequence cycles
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>cache_size</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Cache size of the sequence
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>last_value</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       The last sequence value written to disk.  If caching is used,
       this value can be greater than the last value handed out from the
       sequence.
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   The <structfield>last_value</structfield> column will read as null if any of
   the following are true:
   <itemizedlist>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      The sequence has not been read from yet.
     </para>
    </listitem>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      The current user does not have <literal>USAGE</literal> or
      <literal>SELECT</literal> privilege on the sequence.
     </para>
    </listitem>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      The sequence is unlogged and the server is a standby.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </itemizedlist>
  </para>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-settings">
  <title><structname>pg_settings</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-settings">
   <primary>pg_settings</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   The view <structname>pg_settings</structname> provides access to
   run-time parameters of the server.  It is essentially an alternative
   interface to the <link linkend="sql-show"><command>SHOW</command></link>
   and <link linkend="sql-set"><command>SET</command></link> commands.
   It also provides access to some facts about each parameter that are
   not directly available from <link linkend="sql-show"><command>SHOW</command></link>, such as minimum and
   maximum values.
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_settings</structname> Columns</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       Column Type
      </para>
      <para>
       Description
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>name</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Run-time configuration parameter name
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>setting</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Current value of the parameter
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>unit</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Implicit unit of the parameter
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>category</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Logical group of the parameter
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>short_desc</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A brief description of the parameter
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>extra_desc</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Additional, more detailed, description of the parameter
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>context</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Context required to set the parameter's value (see below)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>vartype</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Parameter type (<literal>bool</literal>, <literal>enum</literal>,
       <literal>integer</literal>, <literal>real</literal>, or <literal>string</literal>)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>source</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Source of the current parameter value
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>min_val</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Minimum allowed value of the parameter (null for non-numeric
       values)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>max_val</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Maximum allowed value of the parameter (null for non-numeric
       values)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>enumvals</structfield> <type>text[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Allowed values of an enum parameter (null for non-enum
       values)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>boot_val</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Parameter value assumed at server startup if the parameter is
       not otherwise set
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>reset_val</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Value that <link linkend="sql-reset"><command>RESET</command></link> would reset the parameter to
       in the current session
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>sourcefile</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Configuration file the current value was set in (null for
       values set from sources other than configuration files, or when
       examined by a user who neither is a superuser nor has privileges of
       <literal>pg_read_all_settings</literal>); helpful when using
       <literal>include</literal> directives in configuration files
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>sourceline</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Line number within the configuration file the current value was
       set at (null for values set from sources other than configuration files,
       or when examined by a user who neither is a superuser nor has privileges of
       <literal>pg_read_all_settings</literal>).
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>pending_restart</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       <literal>true</literal> if the value has been changed in the
       configuration file but needs a restart; or <literal>false</literal>
       otherwise.
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   There are several possible values of <structfield>context</structfield>.
   In order of decreasing difficulty of changing the setting, they are:
  </para>

  <variablelist>
   <varlistentry>
    <!-- PGC_INTERNAL -->
    <term><literal>internal</literal></term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      These settings cannot be changed directly; they reflect internally
      determined values.  Some of them may be adjustable by rebuilding the
      server with different configuration options, or by changing options
      supplied to <application>initdb</application>.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
   <varlistentry>
    <!-- PGC_POSTMASTER -->
    <term><literal>postmaster</literal></term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      These settings can only be applied when the server starts, so any change
      requires restarting the server.  Values for these settings are typically
      stored in the <filename>postgresql.conf</filename> file, or passed on
      the command line when starting the server.  Of course, settings with any
      of the lower <structfield>context</structfield> types can also be
      set at server start time.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
   <varlistentry>
    <!-- PGC_SIGHUP -->
    <term><literal>sighup</literal></term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Changes to these settings can be made in
      <filename>postgresql.conf</filename> without restarting the server.
      Send a <systemitem>SIGHUP</systemitem> signal to the postmaster to
      cause it to re-read <filename>postgresql.conf</filename> and apply
      the changes.  The postmaster will also forward the
      <systemitem>SIGHUP</systemitem> signal to its child processes so that
      they all pick up the new value.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
   <varlistentry>
    <!-- PGC_SU_BACKEND -->
    <term><literal>superuser-backend</literal></term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Changes to these settings can be made in
      <filename>postgresql.conf</filename> without restarting the server.
      They can also be set for a particular session in the connection request
      packet (for example, via <application>libpq</application>'s <literal>PGOPTIONS</literal>
      environment variable), but only if the connecting user is a superuser
      or has been granted the appropriate <literal>SET</literal> privilege.
      However, these settings never change in a session after it is started.
      If you change them in <filename>postgresql.conf</filename>, send a
      <systemitem>SIGHUP</systemitem> signal to the postmaster to cause it to
      re-read <filename>postgresql.conf</filename>.  The new values will only
      affect subsequently-launched sessions.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
   <varlistentry>
    <!-- PGC_BACKEND -->
    <term><literal>backend</literal></term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Changes to these settings can be made in
      <filename>postgresql.conf</filename> without restarting the server.
      They can also be set for a particular session in the connection request
      packet (for example, via <application>libpq</application>'s <literal>PGOPTIONS</literal>
      environment variable); any user can make such a change for their session.
      However, these settings never change in a session after it is started.
      If you change them in <filename>postgresql.conf</filename>, send a
      <systemitem>SIGHUP</systemitem> signal to the postmaster to cause it to
      re-read <filename>postgresql.conf</filename>.  The new values will only
      affect subsequently-launched sessions.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
   <varlistentry>
    <!-- PGC_SUSET -->
    <term><literal>superuser</literal></term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      These settings can be set from <filename>postgresql.conf</filename>,
      or within a session via the <command>SET</command> command; but only superusers
      and users with the appropriate <literal>SET</literal> privilege
      can change them via <command>SET</command>.  Changes in
      <filename>postgresql.conf</filename> will affect existing sessions
      only if no session-local value has been established with <command>SET</command>.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
   <varlistentry>
    <!-- PGC_USERSET -->
    <term><literal>user</literal></term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      These settings can be set from <filename>postgresql.conf</filename>,
      or within a session via the <command>SET</command> command.  Any user is
      allowed to change their session-local value.  Changes in
      <filename>postgresql.conf</filename> will affect existing sessions
      only if no session-local value has been established with <command>SET</command>.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
  </variablelist>

  <para>
   See <xref linkend="config-setting"/> for more information about the various
   ways to change these parameters.
  </para>

  <para>
   This view cannot be inserted into or deleted from, but it can be updated.  An
   <command>UPDATE</command> applied to a row of <structname>pg_settings</structname>
   is equivalent to executing the <command>SET</command> command on that named
   parameter. The change only affects the value used by the current
   session. If an <command>UPDATE</command> is issued within a transaction
   that is later aborted, the effects of the <command>UPDATE</command> command
   disappear when the transaction is rolled back. Once the surrounding
   transaction is committed, the effects will persist until the end of the
   session, unless overridden by another <command>UPDATE</command> or
   <command>SET</command>.
  </para>

  <para>
   This view does not
   display <link linkend="runtime-config-custom">customized options</link>
   unless the extension module that defines them has been loaded by the
   backend process executing the query (e.g., via a mention in
   <xref linkend="guc-shared-preload-libraries"/>,
   a call to a C function in the extension, or the
   <link linkend="sql-load"><command>LOAD</command></link> command).
   For example, since <link linkend="archive-modules">archive modules</link>
   are normally loaded only by the archiver process not regular sessions,
   this view will not display any customized options defined by such modules
   unless special action is taken to load them into the backend process
   executing the query.
  </para>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-shadow">
  <title><structname>pg_shadow</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-shadow">
   <primary>pg_shadow</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   The view <structname>pg_shadow</structname> exists for backwards
   compatibility: it emulates a catalog that existed in
   <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> before version 8.1.
   It shows properties of all roles that are marked as
   <structfield>rolcanlogin</structfield> in
   <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>.
  </para>

  <para>
   The name stems from the fact that this table
   should not be readable by the public since it contains passwords.
   <link linkend="view-pg-user"><structname>pg_user</structname></link>
   is a publicly readable view on
   <structname>pg_shadow</structname> that blanks out the password field.
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_shadow</structname> Columns</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       Column Type
      </para>
      <para>
       Description
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>usename</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>.<structfield>rolname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       User name
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>usesysid</structfield> <type>oid</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>.<structfield>oid</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       ID of this user
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>usecreatedb</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       User can create databases
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>usesuper</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       User is a superuser
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>userepl</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       User can initiate streaming replication and put the system in and
       out of backup mode.
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>usebypassrls</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       User bypasses every row-level security policy, see
       <xref linkend="ddl-rowsecurity"/> for more information.
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>passwd</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Encrypted password; null if none.  See
       <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>
       for details of how encrypted passwords are stored.
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>valuntil</structfield> <type>timestamptz</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Password expiry time (only used for password authentication)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>useconfig</structfield> <type>text[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Session defaults for run-time configuration variables
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-shmem-allocations">
  <title><structname>pg_shmem_allocations</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-shmem-allocations">
   <primary>pg_shmem_allocations</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   The <structname>pg_shmem_allocations</structname> view shows allocations
   made from the server's main shared memory segment.  This includes both
   memory allocated by <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> itself and memory
   allocated by extensions using the mechanisms detailed in
   <xref linkend="xfunc-shared-addin" />.
  </para>

  <para>
   Note that this view does not include memory allocated using the dynamic
   shared memory infrastructure.
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_shmem_allocations</structname> Columns</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       Column Type
      </para>
      <para>
       Description
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>name</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       The name of the shared memory allocation. NULL for unused memory
       and <literal>&lt;anonymous&gt;</literal> for anonymous
       allocations.
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>off</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       The offset at which the allocation starts. NULL for anonymous
       allocations, since details related to them are not known.
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>size</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Size of the allocation in bytes
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>allocated_size</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Size of the allocation in bytes including padding. For anonymous
       allocations, no information about padding is available, so the
       <literal>size</literal> and <literal>allocated_size</literal> columns
       will always be equal. Padding is not meaningful for free memory, so
       the columns will be equal in that case also.
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   Anonymous allocations are allocations that have been made
   with <literal>ShmemAlloc()</literal> directly, rather than via
   <literal>ShmemInitStruct()</literal> or
   <literal>ShmemInitHash()</literal>.
  </para>

  <para>
   By default, the <structname>pg_shmem_allocations</structname> view can be
   read only by superusers or roles with privileges of the
   <literal>pg_read_all_stats</literal> role.
  </para>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-shmem-allocations-numa">
  <title><structname>pg_shmem_allocations_numa</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-shmem-allocations-numa">
   <primary>pg_shmem_allocations_numa</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   The <structname>pg_shmem_allocations_numa</structname> shows how shared
   memory allocations in the server's main shared memory segment are distributed
   across NUMA nodes. This includes both memory allocated by
   <productname>PostgreSQL</productname> itself and memory allocated
   by extensions using the mechanisms detailed in
   <xref linkend="xfunc-shared-addin" />. This view will output multiple rows
   for each of the shared memory segments provided that they are spread across
   multiple NUMA nodes. This view should not be queried by monitoring systems
   as it is very slow and may end up allocating shared memory in case it was not
   used earlier.
   Current limitation for this view is that won't show anonymous shared memory
   allocations.
  </para>

  <para>
   Note that this view does not include memory allocated using the dynamic
   shared memory infrastructure.
  </para>

  <warning>
    <para>
      When determining the <acronym>NUMA</acronym> node, the view touches
      all memory pages for the shared memory segment. This will force
      allocation of the shared memory, if it wasn't allocated already,
      and the memory may get allocated in a single <acronym>NUMA</acronym>
      node (depending on system configuration).
    </para>
  </warning>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_shmem_allocations_numa</structname> Columns</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       Column Type
      </para>
      <para>
       Description
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>name</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       The name of the shared memory allocation.
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>numa_node</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
      ID of <acronym>NUMA</acronym> node
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>size</structfield> <type>int8</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Size of the allocation on this particular NUMA memory node in bytes
      </para></entry>
     </row>

    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   By default, the <structname>pg_shmem_allocations_numa</structname> view can be
   read only by superusers or roles with privileges of the
   <literal>pg_read_all_stats</literal> role.
  </para>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-stats">
  <title><structname>pg_stats</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-stats">
   <primary>pg_stats</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   The view <structname>pg_stats</structname> provides access to
   the information stored in the <link
   linkend="catalog-pg-statistic"><structname>pg_statistic</structname></link>
   catalog.  This view allows access only to rows of
   <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic"><structname>pg_statistic</structname></link> that correspond to tables the
   user has permission to read, and therefore it is safe to allow public
   read access to this view.
  </para>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_stats</structname> is also designed to present the
   information in a more readable format than the underlying catalog
   &mdash; at the cost that its schema must be extended whenever new slot types
   are defined for <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic"><structname>pg_statistic</structname></link>.
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_stats</structname> Columns</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       Column Type
      </para>
      <para>
       Description
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>schemaname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>nspname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of schema containing table
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>tablename</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>relname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of table
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>attname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-attribute"><structname>pg_attribute</structname></link>.<structfield>attname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of column described by this row
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>inherited</structfield> <type>bool</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       If true, this row includes values from child tables, not just the
       values in the specified table
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>null_frac</structfield> <type>float4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Fraction of column entries that are null
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>avg_width</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Average width in bytes of column's entries
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>n_distinct</structfield> <type>float4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       If greater than zero, the estimated number of distinct values in the
       column.  If less than zero, the negative of the number of distinct
       values divided by the number of rows.  (The negated form is used when
       <command>ANALYZE</command> believes that the number of distinct values is
       likely to increase as the table grows; the positive form is used when
       the column seems to have a fixed number of possible values.)  For
       example, -1 indicates a unique column in which the number of distinct
       values is the same as the number of rows.
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>most_common_vals</structfield> <type>anyarray</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of the most common values in the column. (Null if
       no values seem to be more common than any others.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>most_common_freqs</structfield> <type>float4[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of the frequencies of the most common values,
       i.e., number of occurrences of each divided by total number of rows.
       (Null when <structfield>most_common_vals</structfield> is.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>histogram_bounds</structfield> <type>anyarray</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of values that divide the column's values into groups of
       approximately equal population.  The values in
       <structfield>most_common_vals</structfield>, if present, are omitted from this
       histogram calculation.  (This column is null if the column data type
       does not have a <literal>&lt;</literal> operator or if the
       <structfield>most_common_vals</structfield> list accounts for the entire
       population.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>correlation</structfield> <type>float4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Statistical correlation between physical row ordering and
       logical ordering of the column values.  This ranges from -1 to +1.
       When the value is near -1 or +1, an index scan on the column will
       be estimated to be cheaper than when it is near zero, due to reduction
       of random access to the disk.  (This column is null if the column data
       type does not have a <literal>&lt;</literal> operator.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>most_common_elems</structfield> <type>anyarray</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of non-null element values most often appearing within values of
       the column. (Null for scalar types.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>most_common_elem_freqs</structfield> <type>float4[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of the frequencies of the most common element values, i.e., the
       fraction of rows containing at least one instance of the given value.
       Two or three additional values follow the per-element frequencies;
       these are the minimum and maximum of the preceding per-element
       frequencies, and optionally the frequency of null elements.
       (Null when <structfield>most_common_elems</structfield> is.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>elem_count_histogram</structfield> <type>float4[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A histogram of the counts of distinct non-null element values within the
       values of the column, followed by the average number of distinct
       non-null elements.  (Null for scalar types.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>range_length_histogram</structfield> <type>anyarray</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A histogram of the lengths of non-empty and non-null range values of a
       range type column. (Null for non-range types.)
      </para>
      <para>
       This histogram is calculated using the <function>subtype_diff</function>
       range function regardless of whether range bounds are inclusive.
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>range_empty_frac</structfield> <type>float4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Fraction of column entries whose values are empty ranges.
       (Null for non-range types.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>range_bounds_histogram</structfield> <type>anyarray</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A histogram of lower and upper bounds of non-empty and non-null range
       values. (Null for non-range types.)
      </para>
      <para>
       These two histograms are represented as a single array of ranges, whose
       lower bounds represent the histogram of lower bounds, and upper bounds
       represent the histogram of upper bounds.
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   The maximum number of entries in the array fields can be controlled on a
   column-by-column basis using the <link linkend="sql-altertable"><command>ALTER
   TABLE SET STATISTICS</command></link>
   command, or globally by setting the
   <xref linkend="guc-default-statistics-target"/> run-time parameter.
  </para>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-stats-ext">
  <title><structname>pg_stats_ext</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-stats-ext">
   <primary>pg_stats_ext</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   The view <structname>pg_stats_ext</structname> provides access to
   information about each extended statistics object in the database,
   combining information stored in the <link
   linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext"><structname>pg_statistic_ext</structname></link>
   and <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext-data"><structname>pg_statistic_ext_data</structname></link>
   catalogs.  This view allows access only to rows of
   <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext"><structname>pg_statistic_ext</structname></link> and <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext-data"><structname>pg_statistic_ext_data</structname></link>
   that correspond to tables the user owns, and therefore
   it is safe to allow public read access to this view.
  </para>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_stats_ext</structname> is also designed to present the
   information in a more readable format than the underlying catalogs
   &mdash; at the cost that its schema must be extended whenever new types
   of extended statistics are added to <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext"><structname>pg_statistic_ext</structname></link>.
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_stats_ext</structname> Columns</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       Column Type
      </para>
      <para>
       Description
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>schemaname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>nspname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of schema containing table
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>tablename</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>relname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of table
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>statistics_schemaname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>nspname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of schema containing extended statistics object
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>statistics_name</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext"><structname>pg_statistic_ext</structname></link>.<structfield>stxname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of extended statistics object
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>statistics_owner</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>.<structfield>rolname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Owner of the extended statistics object
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>attnames</structfield> <type>name[]</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-attribute"><structname>pg_attribute</structname></link>.<structfield>attname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Names of the columns included in the extended statistics object
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>exprs</structfield> <type>text[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Expressions included in the extended statistics object
      </para></entry>
      </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>kinds</structfield> <type>char[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Types of extended statistics object enabled for this record
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>inherited</structfield> <type>bool</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext-data"><structname>pg_statistic_ext_data</structname></link>.<structfield>stxdinherit</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       If true, the stats include values from child tables, not just the
       values in the specified relation
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>n_distinct</structfield> <type>pg_ndistinct</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       N-distinct counts for combinations of column values. If greater
       than zero, the estimated number of distinct values in the combination.
       If less than zero, the negative of the number of distinct values divided
       by the number of rows.
       (The negated form is used when <command>ANALYZE</command> believes that
       the number of distinct values is likely to increase as the table grows;
       the positive form is used when the column seems to have a fixed number
       of possible values.)  For example, -1 indicates a unique combination of
       columns in which the number of distinct combinations is the same as the
       number of rows.
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>dependencies</structfield> <type>pg_dependencies</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Functional dependency statistics
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>most_common_vals</structfield> <type>text[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of the most common combinations of values in the columns.
       (Null if no combinations seem to be more common than any others.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>most_common_val_nulls</structfield> <type>bool[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of NULL flags for the most common combinations of values.
       (Null when <structfield>most_common_vals</structfield> is.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>most_common_freqs</structfield> <type>float8[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of the frequencies of the most common combinations,
       i.e., number of occurrences of each divided by total number of rows.
       (Null when <structfield>most_common_vals</structfield> is.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>most_common_base_freqs</structfield> <type>float8[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of the base frequencies of the most common combinations,
       i.e., product of per-value frequencies.
       (Null when <structfield>most_common_vals</structfield> is.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   The maximum number of entries in the array fields can be controlled on a
   column-by-column basis using the <link linkend="sql-altertable"><command>ALTER
   TABLE SET STATISTICS</command></link> command, or globally by setting the
   <xref linkend="guc-default-statistics-target"/> run-time parameter.
  </para>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-stats-ext-exprs">
  <title><structname>pg_stats_ext_exprs</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-stats-ext-exprs">
   <primary>pg_stats_ext_exprs</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   The view <structname>pg_stats_ext_exprs</structname> provides access to
   information about all expressions included in extended statistics objects,
   combining information stored in the <link
   linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext"><structname>pg_statistic_ext</structname></link>
   and <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext-data"><structname>pg_statistic_ext_data</structname></link>
   catalogs.  This view allows access only to rows of
   <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext"><structname>pg_statistic_ext</structname></link> and <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext-data"><structname>pg_statistic_ext_data</structname></link>
   that correspond to tables the user owns, and therefore
   it is safe to allow public read access to this view.
  </para>

  <para>
   <structname>pg_stats_ext_exprs</structname> is also designed to present
   the information in a more readable format than the underlying catalogs
   &mdash; at the cost that its schema must be extended whenever the structure
   of statistics in <structname>pg_statistic_ext</structname> changes.
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_stats_ext_exprs</structname> Columns</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       Column Type
      </para>
      <para>
       Description
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>schemaname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>nspname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of schema containing table
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>tablename</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>relname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of table the statistics object is defined on
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>statistics_schemaname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>nspname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of schema containing extended statistics object
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>statistics_name</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext"><structname>pg_statistic_ext</structname></link>.<structfield>stxname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of extended statistics object
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>statistics_owner</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-authid"><structname>pg_authid</structname></link>.<structfield>rolname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Owner of the extended statistics object
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>expr</structfield> <type>text</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Expression included in the extended statistics object
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>inherited</structfield> <type>bool</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-statistic-ext-data"><structname>pg_statistic_ext_data</structname></link>.<structfield>stxdinherit</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       If true, the stats include values from child tables, not just the
       values in the specified relation
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>null_frac</structfield> <type>float4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Fraction of expression entries that are null
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>avg_width</structfield> <type>int4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Average width in bytes of expression's entries
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>n_distinct</structfield> <type>float4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       If greater than zero, the estimated number of distinct values in the
       expression.  If less than zero, the negative of the number of distinct
       values divided by the number of rows.  (The negated form is used when
       <command>ANALYZE</command> believes that the number of distinct values is
       likely to increase as the table grows; the positive form is used when
       the expression seems to have a fixed number of possible values.)  For
       example, -1 indicates a unique expression in which the number of distinct
       values is the same as the number of rows.
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>most_common_vals</structfield> <type>anyarray</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of the most common values in the expression. (Null if
       no values seem to be more common than any others.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>most_common_freqs</structfield> <type>float4[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of the frequencies of the most common values,
       i.e., number of occurrences of each divided by total number of rows.
       (Null when <structfield>most_common_vals</structfield> is.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>histogram_bounds</structfield> <type>anyarray</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of values that divide the expression's values into groups of
       approximately equal population.  The values in
       <structfield>most_common_vals</structfield>, if present, are omitted from this
       histogram calculation.  (This expression is null if the expression data type
       does not have a <literal>&lt;</literal> operator or if the
       <structfield>most_common_vals</structfield> list accounts for the entire
       population.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>correlation</structfield> <type>float4</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       Statistical correlation between physical row ordering and
       logical ordering of the expression values.  This ranges from -1 to +1.
       When the value is near -1 or +1, an index scan on the expression will
       be estimated to be cheaper than when it is near zero, due to reduction
       of random access to the disk.  (This expression is null if the expression's
       data type does not have a <literal>&lt;</literal> operator.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>most_common_elems</structfield> <type>anyarray</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of non-null element values most often appearing within values of
       the expression. (Null for scalar types.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>most_common_elem_freqs</structfield> <type>float4[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A list of the frequencies of the most common element values, i.e., the
       fraction of rows containing at least one instance of the given value.
       Two or three additional values follow the per-element frequencies;
       these are the minimum and maximum of the preceding per-element
       frequencies, and optionally the frequency of null elements.
       (Null when <structfield>most_common_elems</structfield> is.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>elem_count_histogram</structfield> <type>float4[]</type>
      </para>
      <para>
       A histogram of the counts of distinct non-null element values within the
       values of the expression, followed by the average number of distinct
       non-null elements.  (Null for scalar types.)
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </tbody>
   </tgroup>
  </table>

  <para>
   The maximum number of entries in the array fields can be controlled on a
   column-by-column basis using the <link linkend="sql-altertable"><command>ALTER
   TABLE SET STATISTICS</command></link> command, or globally by setting the
   <xref linkend="guc-default-statistics-target"/> run-time parameter.
  </para>

 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="view-pg-tables">
  <title><structname>pg_tables</structname></title>

  <indexterm zone="view-pg-tables">
   <primary>pg_tables</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
   The view <structname>pg_tables</structname> provides access to
   useful information about each table in the database.
  </para>

  <table>
   <title><structname>pg_tables</structname> Columns</title>
   <tgroup cols="1">
    <thead>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       Column Type
      </para>
      <para>
       Description
      </para></entry>
     </row>
    </thead>

    <tbody>
     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>schemaname</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-namespace"><structname>pg_namespace</structname></link>.<structfield>nspname</structfield>)
      </para>
      <para>
       Name of schema containing table
      </para></entry>
     </row>

     <row>
      <entry role="catalog_table_entry"><para role="column_definition">
       <structfield>tablename</structfield> <type>name</type>
       (references <link linkend="catalog-pg-class"><structname>pg_class</structname></link>.<structfield>relname</structfield>)
